From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: R5900: Use the FPU

The R5900 FPU has 32 single precision registers and no double format.
It does not follow IEEE 754: no NaN, no infinity, no denormals, and it
rounds toward zero. The PlayStation 2 port kept it off and emulated
every FPU instruction in software, which costs about 10 us a time.

Turn it on. The R3000 style context code (CPU_R2300_FPU, 32-bit loads
and stores) is already selected for this CPU, and the ELF loader accepts
single float binaries. User space built with -march=r5900 -msingle-float
runs its float math on the FPU and its double math in software. A build
that uses double precision instructions (-march=mips3 with hard float)
must not run on this kernel without "nofpu" on the command line, which
keeps the emulation.


Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port]
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ps2/cpu-feature-overrides.h |  1 -
 arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c                           | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ps2/cpu-feature-overrides.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ps2/cpu-feature-overrides.h
index 4c42474..eafea5c 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ps2/cpu-feature-overrides.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ps2/cpu-feature-overrides.h
@@ -30,7 +30,6 @@
 #define cpu_has_ejtag			0
 #define cpu_has_ic_fills_f_dc		0
 #define cpu_has_inclusive_pcaches	0
-#define cpu_has_fpu 			0	/* FIXME */
 #define cpu_has_toshiba_mmi		1	/* FIXME */
 
 #endif /* __ASM_MACH_PS2_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H */
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
index cd5097e..6169e33 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -1472,7 +1472,15 @@ static inline void cpu_probe_legacy(struct cpuinfo_mips *c, unsigned int cpu)
 		__cpu_name[cpu] = "R5900";
 		c->isa_level = MIPS_CPU_ISA_III;
 		c->fpu_msk31 |= FPU_CSR_CONDX;
-		c->options = R4K_OPTS | MIPS_CPU_DIVEC;
+		/*
+		 * The FPU has 32 single precision registers and no double
+		 * format. It does not follow IEEE 754: no NaN, no infinity,
+		 * no denormals, and it rounds toward zero. User space built
+		 * with -march=r5900 -msingle-float uses it. "nofpu" on the
+		 * kernel command line keeps the software emulation instead.
+		 */
+		c->options = R4K_OPTS | MIPS_CPU_DIVEC | MIPS_CPU_FPU |
+			     MIPS_CPU_32FPR;
 		c->tlbsize = 48;
 		break;
 	case PRID_IMP_NEVADA:
